No. I usually have at least one hundred bullets when I enter
Demogorgon's level. Normally, I need to hit him at most three times with
five bullets from my trusty assault rifle. He moves essentially on every
turn, so he is in line of attack every three turns at least, with very
high probability. I need one and a half to two turns to kill him.

> In Vanilla I used the boulder fort approach in case of the non E-word
> respecting _human_ quest nemeses. 
Yes. In slashem, it is only Demogorgon and Vecna that I urually approach
that way. In the case of Vecna (a non-genocidable Lich), it is even more
necessary, because he can have an insane number of hit points
(approaching 400) and is immune against a lot of stuff. (The exceptions
are magic missile and acid stream, but he regenerates, so you have to
deal a lot of damage in a short time. In fact, you want to kill him for
his hand giving you hungerless regeneration and half physical damage.)

Quest nemeses can usually be beaten in melee. Of course, there are some
where melee is not advisable (if they are wielding the Tsurugi, for
example).
> There it happened to me that he was
> too often in unreachable spots for missiles. But since Demogorgon
> respects the E-word he's much easier to counter; no necessity for a
