If he gets in a single stunning attack, you may be dead. And that will
usually happen when you go downstairs, unless you get the timing right.
Since I have problems getting the timing right all the time, I prefer to
play it safe. I mean I never have problems with that approach in real
game. In explore mode, I have tried other approaches and he did manage
to kill me sometimes. Maybe he is at least a little harder in slashem
than in vanilla. At least he is at a much higher level (106 instead of 50).

Also, he can summon other monsters, so I'd have to deal with those when
not protected by a boulder fort.

> I'd think a permanent E-word would simply solve the issue, then.

Often, yes. But sometimes he would kill my character. And since I have
yet to die the first time after reaching the castle, an event that I do
not anticipate, I prefer to be a bit overprepared. Of course, he becomes
so easy with my approach that the makers of the game may decide at some
point to remove that option. (They could give him the capability to
phase into boulders. And if in addition they make him disregard
Elbereth, I will probably quit the game... :-) )

